# obsidian-tc's local cache/trace dir. The default cacheDir is now ~/.obsidian-tc (absolute), but a
# CLI run with a relative cacheDir can still drop one here — ignore it so a stray cache.db (multi-MB)
# is never accidentally committed.
.obsidian-tc/

# docker-compose.yml's config bind-mount target (THE-638). A contributor copies
# examples/config.scratch.json here and points it at their own vault path — never commit that.
/config/

# Agent tooling. Local STATE stays out; SHARED config is committed.
#
# `.claude/` was blanket-ignored, which meant the project's Claude Code configuration could not
# exist in the repo at all — every hook, skill and convention lived in one contributor's home
# directory and did not travel. The four negations below are checked in deliberately; everything
# else under .claude/ (settings.local.json, state/, caches) stays local, which is what this rule
# was actually protecting.
#
# This does NOT affect the packed .mcpb: .mcpbignore excludes .claude/ independently, so THE-276's
# fix (local state must never reach the distributable) holds regardless of what git tracks.
.omc/
.claude/*
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/agents/
!.claude/hooks/
!.claude/skills/

# graphify knowledge-graph build output (`/graphify`). Generated and rebuildable, multi-MB
# (graph.json alone is ~7 MB), and machine-specific: the manifest and extraction cache key on
# absolute scan-root paths, so a committed copy would be stale for every other checkout and would
# churn the diff on every rebuild.
graphify-out/

# Internal THE-233 migration-planning doc — kept local/private, never published.
MERGE-PROGRESS.md

# The golden set maps queries to REAL note paths in a personal vault — it is a map of that vault's
# contents (folder taxonomy, note titles, and what the author writes about). It is private data, not
# source. Keep it local; commit only multi-hop-golden-set.example.yaml.
packages/server/eval/multi-hop-golden-set.yaml
# THE-652: the SYNTHETIC slice generator writes a corpus beside its yaml. Synthetic, so this is
# repo-bloat insurance rather than a leak guard — but 600+ generated notes should never land here.
packages/server/eval/generated-slice/
packages/server/eval/*-golden-set*.yaml
!packages/server/eval/multi-hop-golden-set.example.yaml
packages/server/eval/baseline.json

# eval/history.ts run store + its static export. Generated, and derived from the private golden
# set above — the run store keeps each recorded artifact verbatim, so it inherits that data's
# privacy even though the artifacts themselves hold only query ids and numbers.
packages/server/eval/runs.db
packages/server/eval/runs.db-*
packages/server/eval/history.html

# generated at build by packages/server/scripts/copy-assets.mjs (source of truth: root SKILLS.md)
packages/server/SKILLS.md

# transient: ci-install-smoke tarball guard extract dir
.tarball-check/
.firecrawl/

# THE-459 perf harness report artifact (generated by `bun run perf`/`perf:gate`; never committed)
packages/server/perf-report.json
# THE-494 Node portability run: the node-targeted bundle and its informational report. Neither is
# a baseline — the gated numbers come from the bun path only.
packages/server/eval/perf/.node-parity.mjs
packages/server/eval/perf/.node-parity.mjs.map
packages/server/perf-node-parity.json

# Linear ticket dump fetched by scripts/fetch-linear-tickets.mjs for the ticket-drift gate.
# This repo is PUBLIC and cites bare THE-nnn ids in source comments deliberately (the gate parses
# them), but this file is different in kind: it carries ticket TITLES and DESCRIPTIONS. Untracked
# by habit until now, which left it one `git add -A` away from publishing the tracker's contents.
packages/server/open-tickets.json
open-tickets.json
